DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_20E5_E69F';
<p>20e5_e69f</p> <p><strong>Duchenne muscular dystrophy (DMD) </strong> is an X-linked recessive genetic disorder that is caused by mutations in the DMD gene. This results in dystrophin is responsible for connecting the actin cytoskeleton to the extracellular matrix (ECM) in muscle cells. The disorder affects 1 in 20,000 males. Individuals affected with DMD have muscle weakness, trouble standing up, which eventually leads to loss of skeletal muscle control, respiratory failure, and death. The defective gene for DMD is located on the short arm of chromosome X at position 21.2. </p><p><strong>Huntington's disease (HD) </strong> is an autosomal dominant genetic disorder that is caused by an increase in trinucleotide repeats in the HTT gene. This results in a mutated Huntington protein that is toxic to certain cell types, particularly brain cells. The disorder affects 1 in 10,000 adults of European descent. Individuals affected with HD have physical abilities that gradually worsen and mental abilities that decline into dementia. The defective gene for HD is located on the short arm of chromosome 4 at position 16.3. </p><p>A man (&male;) and a woman (&female;) are planning a family. The man (&male;) does not have DMD. The woman (&female;) is a carrier for DMD; her father has DMD, but her mother does not. The man (&male;) does not have HD. The woman (&female;) has HD. The father (&male;) of the woman (&female;) does not have HD.</p><p>Reminder: DMD is X-linked recessive and HD is autosomal dominant.</p><p>What fraction of their daughters (&female;) will have DMD but not HD?</p>
PROMPT_20E5_E69F
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_1';
None, 0%
LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_2';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_3';
1/2, 50%
LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_4';
3/4, 75%
LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_5';
All, 100%
LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CORRECT_1';
None, 0%
LITERAL_20E5_E69F_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
